From: Denys Vitali <denys@denv.it>
Subject: [PATCH] egl/wayland: pvr: MESA_PVR_WAYLAND_HW=0 makes clients use swrast

EGL Wayland clients render on the SGX540 by default. With window animations
on, a client's exit can still crash gnome-shell inside the closed SGX blob
(pmos-galaxy docs/bringup.md B17), so MESA_PVR_WAYLAND_HW=0 switches clients to
swrast + wl_shm. The GBM platform (the compositor) is unaffected.
---
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_wayland.c	2026-11-20 00:20:59.633863558 +0000
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_wayland.c	2026-11-20 00:20:59.733862238 +0000
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@
 #include "loader.h"
 #include "util/u_vector.h"
 #include "util/anon_file.h"
+#include "util/debug.h"
 #include "eglglobals.h"
 
 #include <wayland-egl-backend.h>
@@ -2151,7 +2152,12 @@
 EGLBoolean
 dri2_initialize_wayland(_EGLDisplay *disp)
 {
-   if (disp->Options.ForceSoftware)
+   /* pvr: MESA_PVR_WAYLAND_HW=0 makes Wayland clients render with swrast and
+    * present through wl_shm. Client GPU buffers can crash gnome-shell inside
+    * the SGX blob when window animations are on. pmos-galaxy docs/bringup.md
+    * B17. */
+   if (disp->Options.ForceSoftware ||
+       !env_var_as_boolean("MESA_PVR_WAYLAND_HW", true))
       return dri2_initialize_wayland_swrast(disp);
    else
       return dri2_initialize_wayland_drm(disp);
